---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 git push -u origin main what is -u here

-u is short for --set-upstream. It links your local main branch to origin/main on GitHub.

After you've run it once, you can use plain git push and git pull on that branch without naming the remote and branch each time. Git also uses the link in git status to tell you things like "Your branch is ahead of 'origin/main' by 2 commits."

You only need -u the first time you push a branch. After that, git push is enough. It does no harm to repeat it. If you ever want to check the link, git branch -vv shows which remote branch each local branch tracks.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def test_has_title(page:Page)

Where does page come from? You never create it yourself. You use pytest with the pytest-playwright plugin.
When pytest sees a test function with a parameter named page, the plugin does this for you:

1. It launches a browser.
2. It opens a fresh tab.
3. It passes that tab into your test as page.
4. It closes everything after the test.

The parameter has to be named exactly page, because pytest matches it by name. This mechanism is called a fixture.
page is the pytest-playwright plugin registers.

┌───────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐
│     Part      │       Used by       │             Purpose             │
├───────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
│ page (name)   │ pytest              │ Decides which fixture to inject │
├───────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
│ : Page (type) │ You and your editor │ Autocomplete and documentation  │
└───────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘

